+
+# Store post covers with the attachments layer
+
+## Context
+
+Posts get an optional cover image: uploaded on create and edit, replaceable,
+removable, deleted with the post, shown on the post page and in the lists.
+Uploads are bytes a stranger chose, so they must not sit under `public/`, which
+is served as-is to anyone.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Covers use the framework's attachments layer (`bunx guren add attachments`)
+  rather than a `cover_path` column and a hand-written file route. `Post`
+  declares one collection, `cover: hasOneAttached({ image: 'allow' })`; one row
+  of `attachments` describes each stored cover.
+- Bytes live on the private `local` disk (`storage/app`, `storage/app/testing`
+  under `NODE_ENV=test`) and are served by the signed delivery route,
+  `GET /attachments/:id/:filename`. The URL names the attachment, not the post,
+  so a replaced, removed or deleted cover's URL answers 404.
+- What is accepted is the app's rule, in `validateCover()`: PNG or JPEG, judged
+  by the file's leading bytes, 2 MB (2 × 1024 × 1024 bytes) at most. It runs in
+  the controller before anything is written, and fails as a 422 on `cover`.
+  The route's body schema does not carry `cover`: it is parsed synchronously
+  and cannot read a file's bytes.
+- The collection is `image: 'allow'`, not `'require'`: a file that passes
+  `validateCover()` is stored even if the runtime cannot decode it, without
+  width and height.
+- `PostResource` exposes `coverUrl: string | null` and requires its record to
+  come from `Post.withAttachments(records, ['cover'])`, so an action that
+  forgets to load the cover does not compile.
+- Cover URLs are signed for 24 hours instead of the default 5 minutes, because
+  Inertia restores page props from history without a server round trip.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Attachment rows are polymorphic and have no foreign key: nothing cascades.
+  `PostController.destroy` calls `Post.purgeAttachments()`, and
+  `bunx guren attachments:prune` sweeps what a crash leaves behind. Any new
+  code path that deletes posts has to purge as well.
+- `coverUrl` expires. It is for rendering a page now; do not store it or send
+  it in mail.
+- A post and its cover are not written in one transaction. `store` deletes the
+  post again if the cover cannot be attached; `update` attaches the cover
+  before it touches the post's text.
+- Every model that declares attachments must be added to `Model.morphMap` in
+  `AttachmentsProvider`, or the prune command leaves its rows alone.
